### F3 — P2: Freeze exact package/episode authorization for tasks added during cutover

Location: supplement `:20`, contrasted with the exact package/patient/episode requirements in `:9` and `:14`.

The cutover selector names source namespace/run/partition and active trigger rules, while allowing a new configured task to be added. Those fields do not uniquely identify the episode, source package, ownership proof or follow-up record. Multiple exact packages/episodes can share them. The closing sentence makes current source-package authorization mandatory before invalidations and receipt aliases, but does not supply the corresponding committed-reference/source-scope proof for the new task created by cutover itself. This leaves two incompatible implementations: fail closed because no active trigger directly names the new ref, or import an unrelated package's task into an existing episode.

Counterexample: active E1 from exact package A has namespace N/run R/partition P/rule concern-v1. Newly installed package B has a different episode E2 and follow-up F2, with the same namespace/run/partition/rule and same owning doctor. The listed cutover predicate matches B for E1, although F2 is not E1's follow-up. `.review-artifacts/source-checks.json` records this finite predicate counterexample; it is not a claim that final runtime code already implements that predicate.

Minimum resolution: define the exact episode/grant/source/package/owner identity and committed reference-resolution predicate for a cutover addition, including how an explicit administrative amendment associates a new task with an existing episode when its old trigger did not name that follow-up. Require active exact hashes, authorized same-patient/run/partition/source/episode closure, actual configured due/owner/policy/escalation equality and no future/uncommitted refs; reject ambiguous duplicate grants or inconsistent shared refs. Retain old tasks/obligations even when their original grant is revoked, but do not treat retained provenance as authority for a new addition. Add same-rule foreign-episode and cross-package/cross-source negative cases plus one explicitly authorized positive addition. No need to invent a deadline or weaken the missing-rule blocker.

